      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven:\n\n---\n\n## Declaring a Long Rest\n\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, instead of selecting two cards to play, a character may declare a long rest — but only if they have **at least two cards in their discard pile**. The long rest counts as their entire turn for the round and is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\n---\n\n## Long Rest Steps (in order)\n\n1. **Lose one card of your choice** from your discard pile, then return the remaining discarded cards to your hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform *Heal* 2, self.** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items.** Items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered. *(optional)*\n\n---\n\n## Key Notes\n\n- You **cannot** play any ability cards on a round you declare a long rest — it replaces your normal turn entirely.\n- Unlike a *short rest*, you **choose** which card to lose (rather than losing one at random).\n- You must have at least two cards in your discard pile to rest at all (either short or long).\n\n*(Rulebook, passage 125)*",
