      "answer": "## *Poison* — Gloomhaven (2nd Edition)\n\n**Definition**\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 [Attack].\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike *Wound*, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n*(Gloomhaven 2e Rulebook, passage 114)*\n\n---\n\n**Interaction with *Heal***\n\nA single *Heal* can remove both *Wound* and *Poison* from a figure at the same time. However, **if *Poison* is present, the hit point increase from that heal is prevented** — the conditions are removed, but no HP is restored.\n\n*(Gloomhaven 2e Rulebook, passage 118)*\n\n---\n\n**Key FAQ Clarifications** *(Gloomhaven 2e FAQ)*\n\n- **Not stackable:** *Poison* cannot be applied twice to the same figure. If multiple sources attempt to add *Poison* in the same attack, only one token is placed. A single *Safeguard* still fully blocks it. *(FAQ passage 29)*\n- **Objectives are immune:** *Poison* (and all other conditions) can never be applied to Objectives. *(FAQ passage 71)*\n- **Immune allies:** You *can* attempt to give *Poison* to an ally who is immune to it — the attempt counts as fulfilled even if the condition doesn't stick. *(FAQ passage 71)*\n- **\"Give\" does not require Line of Sight:** Giving *Poison* to an ally is not a targeted ability, so LoS is not required (though range still cannot be counted through walls). *(FAQ passage 72)*",
